    confidence: 'Higher when full assay protocols, controls and purity data are supplied; lower with headline potencies only, and say which control is missing.',
    sourceIds: ['chem-probes-2015', 'assay-interference-2017', 'pains-2017', 'chembl-2023', 'nih-rigor-guidance'],
    cards: [
      { id: 'cb108-probe-criteria', term: 'Chemical probe quality criteria', kind: 'checklist', tool_scope: 'workspace-artifact', match: ['chemical probe', 'probe criteria', '화학 프로브', '프로브 기준', 'selectivity', 'negative control compound'], source_ids: ['chem-probes-2015'], summary: 'Arrowsmith and colleagues proposed minimum criteria for protein-targeted chemical probes: in vitro potency below about 100 nM, more than 30-fold selectivity over related proteins in the same family, profiling against broad off-target panels, demonstrated on-target activity in cells at around 1 micromolar or below, a close inactive analogue as negative control, and ideally an orthogonal probe. When a document calls a compound a probe or selective, compare each criterion with what is reported and label missing ones needs-review.' },
      { id: 'cb108-interference-triage', term: 'Assay interference triage', kind: 'failure-mode', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['assay interference', 'aggregator', '분석 간섭', '응집체', 'false positive hit', 'frequent hitter'], source_ids: ['assay-interference-2017'], summary: 'A joint ACS editorial warned that any screening-based discovery, in silico or in the laboratory, is susceptible to compounds that act through artefacts such as colloidal aggregation, reactivity, redox activity or spectroscopic interference, and asked for critical controls. Check whether the document reports controls that address each plausible artefact (for example detergent sensitivity for aggregation, counter-screens, orthogonal readouts). Missing controls make the activity claim needs-review, not false.' },
      { id: 'cb108-pains-limits', term: 'PAINS flags: utility and limits', kind: 'method', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['pains', 'substructure filter', '팬어세이 간섭', '구조 필터', 'pan-assay interference', 'nuisance compound'], source_ids: ['pains-2017', 'assay-interference-2017'], summary: 'PAINS substructure patterns flag classes that often behave as interference compounds, but their authors stress limits: patterns were derived from specific assay formats and libraries, a flagged compound can still be a genuine ligand if it behaves well under appropriate controls, and an unflagged compound is not cleared. Treat a match as a reason to ask for evidence, and never as proof either way. This role cannot run the filters itself; it only comments on flags or structures supplied.' },
      { id: 'cb108-hit-validation-ladder', term: 'Hit validation evidence ladder', kind: 'checklist', tool_scope: 'workspace-artifact', match: ['hit validation', 'hit to lead', '히트 검증', '활성 확인', 'orthogonal assay', 'dose response curve'], source_ids: ['pains-2017', 'assay-interference-2017'], summary: 'Rank the evidence behind an active compound: single-point screen only; confirmed concentration-response; activity in an orthogonal assay format; purity confirmed and activity retained on resynthesis or fresh sample, since contaminants including metals can cause activity; direct binding or mechanism evidence; and consistent structure-activity across close analogues. State the highest rung reached with locations. Claims of mechanism or selectivity need the upper rungs; anything less is needs-review.' },
      { id: 'cb108-sar-audit', term: 'Structure-activity claim audit', kind: 'method', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['structure-activity relationship', 'sar', '구조 활성 관계', '유도체', 'analog series', 'activity cliff'], source_ids: ['assay-interference-2017', 'chem-probes-2015'], summary: 'Check that every SAR statement (adding a group increases potency, a scaffold is essential) is supported by matched compounds in the tables measured in the same assay, and that differences exceed assay variability. Flat or erratic SAR across close analogues is a classic sign of non-specific activity, while genuine SAR plus mechanistic study is the most convincing evidence of a specific interaction. Statements without matched comparisons are needs-review; contradicted ones are incorrect.' },
      { id: 'cb108-bioactivity-provenance', term: 'Bioactivity data provenance and comparability', kind: 'checklist', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['chembl', 'bioactivity data', '생리활성 데이터', '데이터 출처', 'ic50 comparison', 'database record'], source_ids: ['chembl-2023'], summary: 'ChEMBL is a manually curated resource whose content now includes deposited datasets as well as values extracted from literature and patents. Values from different sources, assay formats or endpoints (IC50, Ki, percentage inhibition) are not directly comparable. When a document compares its compound with literature or database values, check that endpoint, assay type and target match, and that the source is cited. Never quote a database value or identifier that was not supplied; mark comparisons without provenance needs-review.' },
      { id: 'cb108-chemical-resource-auth', term: 'Chemical resource authentication', kind: 'checklist', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['compound purity', 'compound identity', '화합물 순도', '시약 품질', 'batch', 'supplier'], source_ids: ['nih-rigor-guidance', 'pains-2017'], summary: 'NIH lists specialty chemicals among key resources whose quality can vary between laboratories and over time and therefore needs authentication. For each key compound check whether the document reports source or batch, purity and the method used, and identity confirmation. Activity that disappears with a fresh or purified sample suggests an impurity. Missing purity or identity evidence is a needs-review gap; detailed structure and identifier checks go to the Chemical Identity reviewer (110).' },
      { id: 'cb108-synthesis-boundary', term: 'No synthesis or handling advice', kind: 'boundary', tool_scope: 'reasoning-only', match: ['synthesis route', 'how to make', '합성 경로', '제조 방법', 'reaction conditions', 'scale up'], source_ids: ['chem-probes-2015'], summary: 'This role reviews claims about compounds in documents. It does not propose or explain synthetic routes, reagents, reaction conditions, purification or scale-up, and does not advise on handling or acquiring substances. When asked, it declines that part and keeps to the evidence question, for example which controls or characterisation data would be needed for the claim. Suggestions of analogues are limited to discussing what existing tables show, not designs for new compounds.' },
    ],
